<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Why I like to do Portrait Photography</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Oswald:wght@200..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        body {
            background-color: darkorange;
            color: #fff;
            font-family: 'Oswald', sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            min-height: 100vh;
        }
        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);
            color: red;
            background-color: white;
            padding: 5px;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }
        p {
            font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.3rem);
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .image-grid {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 20px;
            margin-top: 160px;
        }
        .image-grid img {
            width: clamp(120px, 40vw, 250px);
            height: clamp(120px, 40vw, 250px);
            object-fit: contain;
            border: 2px solid #fff;
            border-radius: 4px;
            background: #000;
        }
        @media (max-width: 480px) {
            body { padding: 10px; }
            .image-grid { gap: 10px; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Why I like to do Portrait Photography</h1>
    <p style="font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3vw, 1.6rem); max-width: 800px; margin: 60px auto 0; background-color: black; padding: 10px; border-radius: 10px;">I like doing portrait photography because it lets me capture people's personality, emotions, and confidence in a single moment. It gives me a chance to be creative with lighting, poses, and backgrounds to make every photo unique. I also enjoy helping people feel good about themselves when they see how great they look in the final pictures.</p>
    <div class="image-grid">
        <img src="images/This 1.jpg" alt="Portrait photo 1">
        <img src="images/This 2.jpg" alt="Portrait photo 2">
        <img src="images/This 3.jpg" alt="Portrait photo 3">
        <img src="images/This 4.jpg" alt="Portrait photo 4">
    </div></body>
</html>